          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"nansen-maria-93ea665425fd352f\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":4,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.97,\"analysis\":\"The narrator directly avows that he loves Maria, giving T maximal support. The immediately coordinated promises—loving her in joy and distress and wishing to live and die with her—also make the declaration a strong relational undertaking, supporting P independently. Although the reunion is intensely emotional, the words are presented as a considered, truthful answer to Maria’s request for assurance, not as reflex-like affective discharge; E therefore receives no support.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The isolated sentence “Jeg elsker Dig” is most plainly an avowal, while its strong performative force emerges from the sentence’s immediate continuation and answer-context.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"A directly narrated spoken reply by the first-person narrator to Maria during their reunion.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"Maria asks whether his changed attitude is genuine, durable, and not merely caused by sexual longing. He answers with an emphatic avowal grounded in his habitual restraint, then expands it into an enduring commitment across hardship and ordinary life. The narration explicitly says Maria understands that he speaks truthfully. Her tears and the scene’s rapture establish emotional intensity but do not independently establish expressive/reflexive force.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"E1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Saavist som jeg altid hellere har sagt Dig for lidt end for meget, saavist elsker jeg Dig. Jeg elsker Dig” (“As surely as I have always preferred to tell you too little rather than too much, so surely do I love you. I love you”).\",\"supports\":\"The utterance is framed as a deliberate and strongly warranted avowal of an enduring emotional state, supporting T rather than reflexive E.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"E2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“Jeg elsker Dig i Lyst og i Nød, Hverdage og Festdage. Du er den, jeg vil dø med, men først vil jeg leve meget, meget længe med Dig.”\",\"supports\":\"The extension across joy, distress, ordinary days, and a shared lifetime invokes an enduring relational undertaking, strongly supporting P alongside T.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"E3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Maria first asks whether it is true and not something he will regret or has imagined from longing; afterward she weeps because she understands that he is “taler sandt” (“speaking the truth”).\",\"supports\":\"The question-and-answer structure and explicit truth framing support a deliberate assurance and avowal; they provide no positive evidence of reflex-like production.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"E4\",\"source\":\"supplied_metadata\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The occurrence is identified as an affirmative present-tense explicit love expression with the exact match “Jeg elsker Dig.”\",\"supports\":\"Confirms that the highlighted core is an unnegated present love declaration rather than a hypothetical or grammatically mentioned form.\",\"confidence\":1.0}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T and P naturally capture the core as both a truthful-state avowal and an enduring relational undertaking. The emotional delivery belongs in contextual interpretation and creates no residual need for E or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
      ],
